EXTRA QUESTIONS
Q: What is a confusion matrix? A: A table comparing actual vs predicted labels. It has 4 values: TP, TN, FP, FN. It helps evaluate classifier performance.
Q: What is TP, TN, FP, FN? A: TP = model said Yes, was Yes. TN = model said No, was No. FP = model said Yes, was No (Type I error). FN = model said No, was Yes (Type II error).
Q: Difference between Precision and Recall? A: Precision = TP/(TP+FP), of all predicted positives how many are correct. Recall = TP/(TP+FN), of all actual positives how many did we find.
Q: When to use F1 vs F2 score? A: F1 when precision and recall are equally important. F2 when recall matters more (e.g. medical diagnosis).
Q: Supervised vs unsupervised learning? A: Supervised uses labelled data (Naive Bayes, SVM, Linear Regression). Unsupervised has no labels and finds patterns (K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering).
Q: What is AUC-ROC? A: ROC curve plots TPR vs FPR. AUC is the area under it: 1.0 = perfect, 0.5 = random.
